WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.645
Mr. Scary, the hotel manager, greeted us when we got off the bus.

2
00:00:08.646 --> 00:00:12.901
"Mr. Scary looks scary," I whispered to Molly.

3
00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:18.997
Molly nodded. "He sure looks mysterious," she whispered back.

4
00:00:18.998 --> 00:00:24.936
"Welcome to Shadow Lake Lodge," said Mr. Scary in a deep voice.

5
00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:31.016
"You will be staying in suite 303."

6
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:36.970
When we got to our suite, Bunch immediately started barking.

7
00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:39.892
"It's the red curtains," said Josh.

8
00:00:39.893 --> 00:00:42.652
"Bunch hates the color red."

9
00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:45.567
"But dogs are color-blind," I said.

10
00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:49.422
"To Bunch, everything looks gray."

11
00:00:49.423 --> 00:00:53.119
"Bunch can see colors," Josh insisted.

12
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.872
" Ruff !" barked Bunch again and again at

13
00:00:58.873 --> 00:01:03.467
the curtains. "See, Iggy? Bunch doesn't like the red curtains,"

14
00:01:03.468 --> 00:01:06.982
said Josh. I shrugged. Maybe Josh

15
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:10.781
was right. Our suite didn't have gold curtains or

16
00:01:10.782 --> 00:01:15.890
diamond tables. But it was pretty cool, with a large living room and

17
00:01:15.891 --> 00:01:20.815
three bedrooms. We unpacked and then headed

18
00:01:20.816 --> 00:01:27.871
back downstairs. In the Lake Lounge room a table was loaded with fresh

19
00:01:27.872 --> 00:01:31.724
vegetables. A sign read: "Vegetable Parade for Families

20
00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:36.864
Today! Help Mr. Scary March Your Favorite Vegetables Right into The Soup

21
00:01:36.865 --> 00:01:41.941
Pot!" "Yuck!" said Caswell.

22
00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:43.624
"Vegetables!" I made a face

23
00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:49.271
too. After my last invention, I was pretty sick of vegetables

24
00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:53.754
myself. "Dad, can we hike up to the lookout tower?" asked

25
00:01:53.755 --> 00:01:56.552
Josh. "Sure," said Mr.

26
00:01:56.553 --> 00:01:59.232
Chen. "We'll go right after

27
00:01:59.233 --> 00:02:04.526
lunch." But after lunch Caswell fell sound asleep in the Lake

28
00:02:04.527 --> 00:02:08.841
Lounge. "You kids can walk up to the tower," said Mr.

29
00:02:08.842 --> 00:02:10.904
Chen. "I'll stay here with

30
00:02:10.905 --> 00:02:18.147
Caswell. But first I'd better go find a blanket for

31
00:02:18.148 --> 00:02:22.782
him." "Wait until you see my new invention," I said when we got

32
00:02:22.783 --> 00:02:26.245
outside. "What is it?" asked

33
00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:31.436
Jenny. I grinned. "It's something called rainbow trail

34
00:02:31.437 --> 00:02:35.331
pellets. I invented the pellets in case we get lost on the

35
00:02:35.332 --> 00:02:38.472
trail. After all, we're not in the city

36
00:02:38.473 --> 00:02:42.103
anymore. We're deep in the

37
00:02:42.104 --> 00:02:45.601
wilderness." I reached into my pocket and took out four

38
00:02:45.602 --> 00:02:49.553
bags. Each one was filled with brightly colored

39
00:02:49.554 --> 00:02:52.185
pellets. Josh peered at the

40
00:02:52.186 --> 00:02:54.975
bag. "Hey! Those are Sparky's hamster

41
00:02:54.976 --> 00:02:57.617
pellets. But they're all different

42
00:02:57.618 --> 00:03:01.429
colors." "I dyed them with food coloring," I said

43
00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.899
proudly. "That way they'll work

44
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.528
better." "How does this invention work exactly?" asked

45
00:03:08.529 --> 00:03:12.251
Molly. "First you open the bag," I

46
00:03:12.252 --> 00:03:14.437
explained. "Then you put the bag in your

47
00:03:14.438 --> 00:03:18.410
pocket. The pellets will dribble out as we

48
00:03:18.411 --> 00:03:20.741
walk." "I get it," said

49
00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:25.850
Josh. "If we take the wrong trail and get stranded, people can just follow the

50
00:03:25.851 --> 00:03:28.633
pellets!" "Right!" I

51
00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:38.174
said. The four of us started up one of the trails to the lookout

52
00:03:38.175 --> 00:03:42.841
tower. When we reached the top, we were amazed by the

53
00:03:42.842 --> 00:03:47.227
view. "You can see for miles up here!" said

54
00:03:47.228 --> 00:03:52.002
Jenny. "Hey." Josh reached around to check his back pocket.

55
00:03:52.003 --> 00:03:54.735
"My bag of pellets is empty."

56
00:03:54.736 --> 00:03:58.699
"Mine is too," said Molly and Jenny.

57
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.248
I felt in my pocket.

58
00:04:00.249 --> 00:04:03.156
My bag was also empty.

59
00:04:03.157 --> 00:04:06.902
"The pellets worked perfectly!" I declared.

60
00:04:06.903 --> 00:04:10.890
"If we were stranded, people would be able to find us."

61
00:04:10.891 --> 00:04:15.805
"It's another one of Iggy's brilliant inventions!" said Josh.

62
00:04:15.806 --> 00:04:21.503
"I'm glad we're not really stranded though," said Jenny.

63
00:04:21.504 --> 00:04:28.797
We explored the lookout tower for a while and then headed back to the hotel.

64
00:04:28.798 --> 00:04:34.399
When we arrived back at the Lake Lounge room, Caswell was wide-awake.

65
00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.377
He was playing checkers with Mr. Chen.

66
00:04:37.378 --> 00:04:43.485
Nearby Mr. Scary, the hotel manager, was wringing his hands.

67
00:04:43.486 --> 00:04:47.992
"A disaster has happened!" he cried.

68
00:04:47.993 --> 00:04:50.343
"All my vegetables have disappeared!

69
00:04:50.344 --> 00:04:53.603
My vegetable parade is ruined!"

70
00:04:53.604 --> 00:04:55.966
Mr. Scary was right.

71
00:04:55.967 --> 00:05:00.207
The vegetables for the parade had vanished.

72
00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:05.713
"I will find the thief who stole my vegetables," cried Mr. Scary.

73
00:05:05.714 --> 00:05:11.417
"And I will punish him!"

